{
    "word": "picaresque",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "bb7c9ebe-7d6d-3da9-a2d7-580fe0bc4ea4",
                "word": "picaresque",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "85ec432b-2498-48ca-99e8-f90bb48d144a",
                        "entry_id": "bb7c9ebe-7d6d-3da9-a2d7-580fe0bc4ea4",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more picaresque"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "0d875d80-0e8b-4568-943c-9b720e82fd89",
                        "entry_id": "bb7c9ebe-7d6d-3da9-a2d7-580fe0bc4ea4",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most picaresque"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1a857783-80fc-3ed6-b4cb-51dccfcb0a18",
                        "entry_id": "bb7c9ebe-7d6d-3da9-a2d7-580fe0bc4ea4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or pertaining to adventurers or rogues."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cbe95d3f-96a6-49d9-a4b9-668ae22aad22",
                                "sense_id": "1a857783-80fc-3ed6-b4cb-51dccfcb0a18",
                                "text": "The blue and white of the Murano background and the frankly picaresque tramp seem to form strange bed-fellows for the supper-party below stairs into which any gentleman's gentleman of the siècle de Dr. [Samuel] Johnson might have walked at any moment. [Describing an adaptation of Carlo Goldoni's The Servant of Two Masters (1746).]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "eb493262-c93f-3aaa-acaf-f5c183ea09c4",
                        "entry_id": "bb7c9ebe-7d6d-3da9-a2d7-580fe0bc4ea4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Characteristic of a genre of Spanish satiric novel dealing with the adventures of a roguish hero."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6dfcb00a-aef9-4fd2-95ae-4366b368a077",
                                "sense_id": "eb493262-c93f-3aaa-acaf-f5c183ea09c4",
                                "text": "A mere piece of roguery told in the abstract, without the proper picaresque ornaments, its manifold sinuosities and dexterities, has no interest for the reader; it may recommend the executor of it to the administration of a cat-o-nine-tails, or to an honourable post in the gallies: but there is no music in it without the proper accompaniments."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5a874809-b39e-4aad-a211-3c7a2e928d6b",
                                "sense_id": "eb493262-c93f-3aaa-acaf-f5c183ea09c4",
                                "text": "Spain became celebrated about the end of this century for her novels in the picaresque style, of which Lazarillo de Tormes is the oldest extant specimen."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c417ba2f-e6f3-42e8-9e38-1dd02e803e5a",
                                "sense_id": "eb493262-c93f-3aaa-acaf-f5c183ea09c4",
                                "text": "He [Daniel Defoe] produced an amazing variety of wares: newspapers, magazines, ghost stories, biographies, journals, memoirs, satires, picaresque romances, essays on religion, reform, trade, projects, – in all more than two hundred works."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d4b257a2-3597-478c-ad8b-323ba6c8e5d0",
                                "sense_id": "eb493262-c93f-3aaa-acaf-f5c183ea09c4",
                                "text": "Opening in France just before the Revolution and concluding just after the attack on the Tuileries, [Rafael] Sabatini's novel deftly combines historical romance, picaresque novel and revenge tragedy."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1fa1a17c-223f-4b5b-81d2-540cd08c9320",
                                "sense_id": "eb493262-c93f-3aaa-acaf-f5c183ea09c4",
                                "text": "The picaresque novel finds its origins in the humanist search for an expansion of the historiographical genre. [...] The protagonist of the picaresque novel is the pícaro, a character of lowly descent who, by passing through a wide array of professions, attempts to rise in social standing."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9afd6bc7-c281-4f64-8d43-97a48b02826b",
                        "source_entry_id": "bb7c9ebe-7d6d-3da9-a2d7-580fe0bc4ea4",
                        "source_sense_description": "of or pertaining to rogues",
                        "target_lang_word": "picaresque",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "picaresque",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3a5161b8-383a-395f-aa8e-e1ac6cd3b216",
                                        "entry_id": "ab7a3c40-3be1-3b5a-9f48-aea8f2cd150f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Genre littéraire d’origine espagnole pratiqué entre le XVIᵉ et le XVIIIᵉ siècle, dont le personnage principal est un aventurier marginal et malhonnête."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5e2f51d3-f093-441e-962c-a70b5f987778",
                                                "sense_id": "3a5161b8-383a-395f-aa8e-e1ac6cd3b216",
                                                "text": "Mais concevoir la psychologie comme une simple affaire de mécanisme, prétendre ne pas tenir compte de la qualité morale des actes ni de leur retentissement intime... voilà qui nous conduit tout droit au picaresque."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "picaresque",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f8c1411f-7d0d-3352-85f9-f7726806095c",
                                        "entry_id": "ff729127-9592-38e7-b9a2-cab20870c28a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "D’un genre littéraire d’origine espagnole pratiqué entre le XVIᵉ et le XVIIIᵉ siècle, dont le personnage principal est un aventurier marginal et malhonnête."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c5052b2-f52d-4ece-8b3f-ca7f0a32bfca",
                                                "sense_id": "f8c1411f-7d0d-3352-85f9-f7726806095c",
                                                "text": "La mode alors était d’ailleurs aux sujets picaresques, et les gens de lettres, qui donnent toujours un peu le ton aux artistes, avaient contribué à lancer la peinture dans cette voie basse et triviale. Les plus grands seigneurs, quand ils daignaient prendre la plume, se complaisaient à décrire les mœurs des filous et des mendiants."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51d738e8-a738-49ec-a416-3e0f0f5cc151",
                                                "sense_id": "f8c1411f-7d0d-3352-85f9-f7726806095c",
                                                "text": "Une tasse de thé clair. On la repose au creux du banc. Sur la porcelaine blanche, le dessin vert foncé figure un décor de campagne arrondi, une diligence picaresque et drôle, mais on n’aperçoit pas Mr Pickwick."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "22c1f790-0597-47b9-8785-604cfa63cc41",
                                                "sense_id": "f8c1411f-7d0d-3352-85f9-f7726806095c",
                                                "text": "L’espion, picaresque, se déguise ; l’éclaireur, épique, ne condescend pas à ces travestissements."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "84a3a7ae-b6a9-49ca-9f14-e8d4369b8b15",
                                                "sense_id": "f8c1411f-7d0d-3352-85f9-f7726806095c",
                                                "text": "L’adaptation du roman picaresque de Pierre Lemaitre, Prix Goncourt en 2013, s’annonçait casse-gueule pour Albert Dupontel : casting cinq étoiles (Dupontel lui-même, Émilie Dequenne, Mélanie Thierry, entre autres), histoire énorme, budget assorti…"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d20fc7b-ba22-4b3a-8bb6-c98c6d4a2f52",
                                                "sense_id": "f8c1411f-7d0d-3352-85f9-f7726806095c",
                                                "text": "Westlake propose là un roman policier dans le plus pur style picaresque. Ce genre est né au milieu du XVIᵉ siècle avec la célèbre Vie de Lazarillo de Tormes. […] La littérature produit beaucoup de romans picaresques dans les périodes troublées."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
